{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "A Serious Image Problem"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Investigating the Rumor"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Explains customs and appropriate behaviour at work and in different countries, using a wider   range of expressions and   formulas."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and specific  information and  aspects of attitude and   intention in   conversations, texts or   presentations about   the communicative   functions related to   this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and specific  information and  aspects of attitude and   intention in   conversations, texts or   presentations about   the communicative   functions related to   this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and specific  information and  aspects of attitude and   intention in   conversations, texts or   presentations about   the communicative   functions related to   this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and specific  information and  aspects of attitude and   intention in   conversations, texts or   presentations about   the communicative   functions related to   this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and specific  information and  aspects of attitude and   intention in   conversations, texts or   presentations about   the communicative   functions related to   this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and specific  information and  aspects of attitude and   intention in   conversations, texts or   presentations about   the communicative   functions related to   this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and specific  information and  aspects of attitude and   intention in   conversations, texts or   presentations about   the communicative   functions related to   this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and specific  information and  aspects of attitude and   intention in   conversations, texts or   presentations about   the communicative   functions related to   this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Making and Responding to Polite Requests"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the modals <span class=\"italic\">can</span>, <span class=\"italic\">could</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would</span> to politely ask someone to do something for you."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Can/Could/Would + you + verb"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: </br><span class=\"italic\">Could you get me a drink?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can also use phrases like:</br><span class=\"italic\">Could you do me a favor?</br>Can I ask you for a favor?</br>Could you do something for me?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "To respond to a polite request you can say:</br><span class=\"italic\">It would be my pleasure. </br>Of course. </br>Absolutely. </br>I'd be happy help you.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I'm sorry. I can't. </br> I would love to, but ...</span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Modal Verb</span>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Polite request</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">can</span></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"polite\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can you do that for me?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">could</span></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more polite\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Could you do me a huge favor?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">would</span></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"most polite\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Would you please get me a drink?</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Would you do me a favor?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Could I ask you to help me with something?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can you do that for me?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Could you also do me a huge favor?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It would be my pleasure. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Gerunds and Infinitives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> is a verb ending with -ing (doing).</br> An<span class=\"strong\"> Infinitive</span> is to + verb (to do). <br></br>There are rules about which verbs you can use with gerunds and which verbs you can use with Infinitives."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Verbs commonly followed by a gerund:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Verbs that express<span class=\"strong\"> likes/dislikes:</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>like <li>love<li> enjoy <li>dislike<li> hate<li> mind</ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: </br><span class=\"italic\"> Would you<span class=\"strong\"> mind getting</span> us a drink?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">like/love/hate</span> can also be followed by an Infinitive</ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Some other verbs that are followed by a gerund:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>anticipate<li> consider<li> delay <li>complete<li> involve<li> suggest<li> risk <li>regret</ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use gerunds after prepositions: </br><span class=\"italic\">Farmani's <span class=\"strong'>relies on employing </span>child labor.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "These are some verbs that are followed by an infinitive:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>hope <li>seem <li>need <li>manage <li>appear<li> deserve<li> expect<li> ask <li>happen</ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: </br> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">manage to mix</span> business with pleasure</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use Infinitives after adjectives.  </br>Example:</br><span class=\"italic\"> I'd be <span class=\"strong\">happy to help </span>you. I was never <span class=\"strong\">able to mind </span>my own business.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I enjoy drinking and chatting."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You deserve to drink something cold in this hot weather."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I didn't expect to see you in Brazil so soon. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll work on getting the truth. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The rumour is that Farmani's agreed to outsource his labor."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "business or pleasure"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "for work or enjoyment, personal happiness"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Did you happen to come here for business or pleasure?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le04ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about jobs and work."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mix business with pleasure"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "combine work and fun"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When I travel abroad, I manage to mix business with pleasure."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le04ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "urgent"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very important"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I regret to inform you that it is urgent business. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le04ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to mind your own business"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to not ask someone private questions"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm never able to mind my own business."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le04ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to investigate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to look for information on a subject"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I need someone to investigate the business practices of a clothing company. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le04ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "business practices"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a set of working methods"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I feel like their business practices are not ethical."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le04ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "labor "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "work"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type